<?xml version="1.0" encoding="utf-8"?>
<Catalog>

    <!-- =====================================================================
         TARDIGRADE: LARVA FALLBACK BUILD BUTTONS

         NOTE: the Larva below is the ONLY unit this file touches. It used to
         carry ~150 lines of AbilArray grants and explicit CardLayouts cells -
         Battle Blink and Medivac Boost on 49 combat units, Salvage on 64
         structures - and all of it is gone, because every drafted modifier is
         a passive or a condition now and none of them puts a button on a
         command card. See AbilData.xml for the rest of that note.

         Keep every comment in this file directly above an element. SC2's
         parser attaches a comment to the element that FOLLOWS it, so a
         trailing comment before </Catalog> warns "m_comment == nullptr".
         The morph units Ravager / Lurker / Brood Lord / Baneling are given a
         direct larva-build path in AbilData.xml (LarvaTrain Train6/9/14/16) so
         they stay buildable even if their morph parent was banned. Those train
         options need command-card buttons on the Larva.

         Each button is placed on its PARENT's cell (Roach / Hydralisk /
         Corruptor / Zergling), and RosterEnforce_GateLarvaFallbacks makes
         sure only one of the two is ever on the card: an undrafted parent's
         button is removed by TechTreeUnitAllow, and a drafted parent gets the
         fallback disallowed instead (the child then morphs from the parent).

         Cells are the parents' real positions in the merged LotV Larva card
         (core -> ... -> voidmulti):
           Row 0: Drone, Overlord, Zergling, Roach, -
           Row 1: Hydralisk, Mutalisk, Corruptor, Infestor, Swarm Host
           Row 2: Viper, Ultralisk, -, -, Cancel
         The first version had Ravager / Lurker / Brood Lord one cell off
         (on Hydralisk, Mutalisk and Ultralisk), so a drafted Hydralisk hid
         the Ravager fallback outright.
    ===================================================================== -->
    <CUnit id="Larva">
        <CardLayouts index="0">
            <LayoutButtons Face="Ravager"   Type="AbilCmd" AbilCmd="LarvaTrain,Train6"  Row="0" Column="3"/>
            <LayoutButtons Face="LurkerMP"  Type="AbilCmd" AbilCmd="LarvaTrain,Train9"  Row="1" Column="0"/>
            <LayoutButtons Face="BroodLord" Type="AbilCmd" AbilCmd="LarvaTrain,Train14" Row="1" Column="2"/>
            <LayoutButtons Face="Baneling"  Type="AbilCmd" AbilCmd="LarvaTrain,Train16" Row="0" Column="2"/>
        </CardLayouts>
    </CUnit>

    <!-- =====================================================================
         TARDIGRADE: ARCHON FALLBACK BUILD BUTTONS

         Same story as the Larva above: AbilData.xml gives GatewayTrain and
         WarpGateTrain a Train8 that builds an Archon directly, but a train
         option with no LayoutButtons entry never reaches a command card, so
         the button was invisible and the fallback unreachable.

         The button sits on the High Templar's cell (Row 1, Column 0 in the
         merged LotV Gateway / Warp Gate card: Zealot, Sentry, Stalker, Adept
         on row 0; High Templar, Dark Templar on row 1). The two can never
         show at once - RosterEnforce_GateArchonFallback disallows Train8
         whenever either templar is drafted, and an undrafted High Templar's
         own button is already removed by TechTreeUnitAllow.
    ===================================================================== -->
    <CUnit id="Gateway">
        <CardLayouts index="0">
            <LayoutButtons Face="Archon" Type="AbilCmd" AbilCmd="GatewayTrain,Train8" Row="1" Column="0"/>
        </CardLayouts>
    </CUnit>

    <CUnit id="WarpGate">
        <CardLayouts index="0">
            <LayoutButtons Face="Archon" Type="AbilCmd" AbilCmd="WarpGateTrain,Train8" Row="1" Column="0"/>
        </CardLayouts>
    </CUnit>

</Catalog>
